commit b504302b7ad20dcd41e58a5e81a7f48be8642a6c
Author: Seth Ford <sethford@studio.local>
Date:   Sat May 16 21:51:15 2026 -0400

    feat(sprint-11): US-11.1 vendor patch for DPO pad masking + length norm
    
    Sprint 11 Wave 0, P0. Eliminates the length-bias-into-pad-collapse
    pathway that Sprint 8 smoke-run-3 surfaced (40% pad-leakage at the
    best iter-60 checkpoint; 80% at iter-200).
    
    Root cause (mlx_lm_lora==2.1.0, trainer/dpo_trainer.py:50-52):
    
        def compute_score(scores, mask, loss_type):
            token_count = mask.sum(-1)
            return scores.sum(-1) / token_count \
                   if loss_type == "ipo" else scores.sum(-1)
    
    For loss_type=="sigmoid" the per-token (pad-masked) log-probs are
    SUMMED, never divided by non-pad count. The optimizer's cheapest move
    is to shorten the rejected sequence by emitting pad early — textbook
    length-bias-into-pad-collapse (SimPO §3, sota-dpo.md §4).
    
    Fix: vendor + monkey-patch, NOT upstream PR (Sprint 11 cannot block on
    multi-week merge timeline).
    
      scripts/mlx_lora_patch.py    apply_length_norm_patch()
                                   version-pinned to {"2.1.0"}, idempotent
                                   replaces compute_score with
                                     (scores * mask).sum(-1)
                                       / mx.maximum(mask.sum(-1), 1.0)
    
      scripts/mlx_lora_entry.py    -m target wrapper; applies the patch then
                                   dispatches to mlx_lm_lora.train.main()
    
      scripts/finetune-gemma.py    --length-normalize (default true) flag;
                                   routes through scripts.mlx_lora_entry;
                                   propagates HU_DPO_LENGTH_NORM env to the
                                   subprocess; records length_normalize in
                                   train_config.json
    
      tests/test_dpo_pad_masking.py
                                   5 unit tests on patched compute_score:
                                     - pad excluded from sum (AC-11.1.1)
                                     - 10/50 length-norm (AC-11.1.2)
                                     - IPO unchanged
                                     - empty-mask no-div-by-zero
                                     - idempotent + version pinned
    
      tests/test_pareto_pad_regression.py
                                   4 Sprint 8 fixture regressions:
                                     - iter-200 broken FAILS gate (AC-11.1.4)
                                     - iter-60 best classified DEFER
                                     - post-patch synthetic PROMOTE
                                     - high-delta-alone REJECT guard
    
      tests/fixtures/sprint8_sweep.json
                                   Transcribed from smoke-run-3.md table +
                                   Smoke #2 iter-200 row. 5 checkpoints.
    
      tests/test_finetune_gemma_dpo.py
                                   Updated -m assertion to scripts.mlx_lora_entry.
                                   Added Path.home monkeypatch on the 2 tests
                                   that find_dpo_data was leaking ~/.human into
                                   (UnicodeDecodeError from real PII bytes).
    
    All 14 tests pass under HU_IS_TEST=1; no model weights loaded.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>

